<title>USA: GM October U.S. car sales fall 24 pct.</title>
<headline>GM October U.S. car sales fall 24 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp</p>
<p>			Oct 1-31, 1996     Oct 1-31, 1995 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Total Car		215,276	   272,830	    -24.0</p>
<p> Total Truck	    187,144	   147,578	    +22.1</p>
<p>		  Jan 1-Oct 31, 1996 Jan 1-Oct 31, 1995 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Total Car	    2,416,644	 2,507,690	     -4.4</p>
<p> Total Truck	  1,693,688	 1,603,454	     +4.8</p>
<p>* Pct change based on daily selling rate. Sale days 27 in latest month vs 26, 258 for year to date vs 256 in year ago.</p>
<p>Results include sales from Saab, a joint venture of GM and Insvestor AB, of 1,478 and 2,359 for October of 1996 and 1995, respectively, and 24,052 and 22,741 in the year-to-date periods.</p>
</text>
